    {
      "text": "SPECTRUM OF THE LAPLACIAN ON THE FRICKE-MACBEATH SURFACE — The Fricke-Macbeath surface is the unique Hurwitz surface of genus 7 with 504 conformal automorphisms.\n\n**SPECTRUM OF THE LAPLACIAN ON THE FRICKE-MACBEATH SURFACE**\n\n*CHUL-HEE LEE*\n\n40 pp, 19 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The Fricke-Macbeath surface is the unique Hurwitz surface of genus 7 with 504 conformal automorphisms. In this paper, we prove that the first eigenvalue of the Laplacian on the Fricke-Macbeath surface has a sevenfold multiplicity and con- tained in the interval [1.23, 1.26]. Further, we numerically identify the 7-dimensional representation of its automorphism group corresponding to the eigenspace associ- ated to the first eigenvalue. We also determine the Dirichlet domain centered at 0 for a Fuchsian group that uniformizes the Fricke-Macbeath surface, identifying the algebraic coordinates for its vertices.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Background; 2.1 Laplacian on Riemannian manifolds; 2.2 Two models of hyperbolic plane; 2.3 Selberg trace formula; 3 Explicit uniformization of the Fricke-Macbea; 3.1 Hurwitz surfaces and the Fricke-Macbeath s; 3.2 Definition of as a subgroup of a Coxeter g; 3.3 Fundamental domain for; 3.4 Length spectrum of the Fricke-Macbeath sur; 4 Multiplicity of the first eigenvalue; 4.1 Overview of the proof; 4.5 Proof of 1[1.23, 1.26] and determination o; 5 Numerical determination of the eigenspace as; Acknowledgements; Appendix A. Word processing in (2,3,7); Appendix B. GAP code for the automorphism grou",
